<title>GERMANY: Metro shares lifted by 96 profits.</title>
<headline>Metro shares lifted by 96 profits.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German retailer Metro AG outperformed on Tuesday as the market welcomed better than expected 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>Metro had posted its first full year profit on ordinary activities of 1.1 billion marks early on Tuesday and issued an optimistic outlook for this year.</p>
<p>One dealer said the numbers were &quot;extraordinarily good.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;I pounced on it,&quot; another said.</p>
<p>Metro led advancers in a mixed market to trade up 6.50 marks, or 3.7 percent, at 184 marks at 0759 GMT and hit a new intraday high of 189.90 marks early in the session.</p>
<p>The broader market was flat.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
